# Generated, and deliberately not committed. See README, "The typed client".
#
# The schema and the types derived from it are a projection of the application at one
# commit. A committed copy is right until the day somebody changes a response model and
# does not rerun the generator, and from then on the console compiles against an API that
# no longer exists while every check stays green. Regenerating is one command and it needs
# no running server, so there is no reason to keep a stale copy for convenience.
src/api/generated/

node_modules/
dist/
*.local

# The console reads only VITE_-prefixed values, and Vite inlines every one of them into
# the bundle in plain text. Nothing secret can live in this file, and the example beside
# it says so. It is ignored anyway, because a per-developer host name is not shared state.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
